            <h4 data-number="5.2.5.3" id="event-place"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.2.5.3</span> Event
            Place</h4>
            <p><strong>Element name:</strong> &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#eventPlace">lido:eventPlace</a>&gt;</p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Event Place contains information
            about the place where the event occured, including
            identifying data, names and possibly coordinates. The type
            of place, whether it is an adminstrative entity such as a
            city or country, or a physical feature such as a river or a
            mountain, can be captured in detail using the &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#placeClassification">lido:placeClassification</a>&gt;
            element.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The following example describes
            the city “Florence” as a possible place of production of the
          